00:49:09,680 --> 00:49:15,280
 of token patterns that will be most frequently seen. So, obviously very common words like

530
00:49:15,280 --> 00:49:21,160
 the me, I, your. So, all of all these kinds of words will be very frequently seen in a

531
00:49:21,160 --> 00:49:26,520
 corpus. So, this would automatically be captured by this tokenization process. So, BPA kind

532
00:49:26,520 --> 00:49:31,800
 of includes the most frequent words by default and it will also have certain constituent

533
00:49:31,800 --> 00:49:37,200
 subwords that would help you to later reconstruct bigger words that you have not seen before.

534
00:49:37,200 --> 00:49:41,960
 So, that allows you to avoid the out of vocab problem when you don't have not seen the vocab

535
00:49:41,960 --> 00:49:49,080
 during printing data and it also kind of allows you to handle that if there is some word like

