00:49:58,280 --> 00:50:04,720
 within that word. So, the BPA tokenizer still contains the individual character and will

539
00:50:04,720 --> 00:50:10,480
 tokenize any unseen words by at least at a character level. So, it can start from full

540
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:15,400
 words then to subwords if it has not seen that and if it's a very novel word that it

541
00:50:15,400 --> 00:50:19,400
 has like not even seen the patterns within it, it will just break it down to all characters

542
00:50:19,400 --> 00:50:24,080
 and it will always allow the transformer model or the language model to have a unique representation

543
00:50:24,080 --> 00:50:33,480
 for those. So, and how is this built is essentially you start with, so you first start with the

544
00:50:33,480 --> 00:50:37,920
 array of all the characters that you want to cover. So, this is for example the character

