00:50:37,920 --> 00:50:44,240
 essentially English alphabet or any other language alphabet and then you start figuring

546
00:50:44,240 --> 00:50:48,520
 out what are the most common patterns that you want to add to the vocab. So, if you have

547
00:50:48,520 --> 00:50:53,920
 the first character, if you first have the characters in your list of vocab, then what

548
00:50:53,920 --> 00:50:58,880
 you can do, you can start looking at pairs of these characters and see which ones are

549
00:50:58,880 --> 00:51:04,600
 next most frequent in the dataset and then you can repeat the process to formulate bigger

550
00:51:04,600 --> 00:51:08,640
 and bigger patterns and then you will also have words and subwords all included in the

551
00:51:08,640 --> 00:51:13,760
 vocab and you can stop at some vocab size V so that you have the most common things

552
00:51:13,760 --> 00:51:18,200
 up until that point included in the vocab and anything that is beyond that will be reconstructed

553
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:25,980
 using the tokenization mechanism. So, basically this BP tokenizer or subword tokenization

554
00:51:25,980 --> 00:51:32,800
 kind of solved a big problem that was lingering for like almost a decade but this didn't solve

555
00:51:32,800 --> 00:51:37,160
 all like many other problems also which are still kind of existing problems and people

556
00:51:37,160 --> 00:51:41,680
 are trying to come up with like intelligent solutions. So, one is that you have to keep

